# U062: independently owned real-browser look-alike fixture

This is verification tooling, not a lifecycle implementation change. The old
standalone Edge fixture mistook a compatibility launcher's PID for its surviving
browser. Both old reader files actually ran all three bodies: each recorded two
passes and a genuine look-alike survival assertion failure. Their failures,
interrupted command endings, original streams, and source epoch remain history.

The replacement opens a separate counter fixture through the unchanged sealed
helper, not the bounded-startup or close subject under test. An authenticated
browser-level CDP connection reports its actual browser PID. Native creation
identities confirm that new root twice; a pre-existing root, changed root,
ambiguous protocol response, or reused PID cannot manufacture ownership.
Only that independently owned session and its recorded native identities are
closed. No image-name sweep, new-process sweep, path-marker ownership, compatibility
disabling flag, sandbox bypass, package installation, or global configuration is used.

## Verification

The retained U005 and U006 fixtures each fail seven of the eight deterministic
requirements while the direct-launch control passes. The assertion bodies then
pass unchanged against the replacement, including handoff, PID reuse, same-image
neighbor protection, idempotent close, protocol detachment, and settled handles.
The portable retained replay changes only the loader location, not the assertions.

Both corrected real files retain all three cases and their original caps. On the
installed Microsoft-signed qualified Edge `157.0.4341.42`, U005 passed 3/3 and U006
passed 3/3, without skips, todos, cancellations, signals, guard timeouts, or manual
process stops. Both TAP summaries and Node processes exited naturally. The saved
records carry the actual independent browser/root creation identity and version.

## Evidence authority and scope

`evidence\u062\authority-base.json` seals the six original verification sources,
all 64 original lifecycle capture manifests, two additional read-only fixture
imports, and the reviewed U061 authority predecessor. Content-addressed original
snapshots retain every old byte. A new numbered addendum and head authorize only
the exact tooling transition and explicit raw/LF/CRLF source representations.
Mixed line endings, unknown manifests, forged recorded input pairs, unregistered
source changes, changed imports, and changed historical captures are refused.
The original verifier still checks every transcript, exit, summary, and unchanged
input; the amendment wrapper removes only a proved exact source-transition error.
The existing fix-evidence assertions are unchanged; their callers now delegate
to that explicitly pinned wrapper, and their original sources are retained.
`imports.json`, U061 heads, all old captures, and all old authority remain unchanged.

The candidate uses only the independently reviewed U061 tooling overlay, not the
unapplied U007 implementation. That overlay is a declared prerequisite baseline,
not work attributed to U062 or an application/acceptance grant.

All six accepted lifecycle implementation files and the isolated/loopback helpers
are unchanged. Coverage is not applicable: every new executable file is verification
tooling under tests or retained evidence. Public command outputs are explicit
portable projections with original private raw hashes recorded separately; they
are never passed off as original raw streams. Unknown shared-runtime neighbors
are preserved, never adopted or deleted.

Only the parent independently reviews, applies, publishes, and marks Done under
the existing U005/U006 scopes. Neither this fixture proof nor reader completion
is U034 qualification completion, lifecycle application, Azure execution, or
publication authority.
